WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.359
The following video tutorial series

2
00:00:03.359 --> 00:00:06.719
is going to be broken up into three main parts.

3
00:00:06.719 --> 00:00:09.880
First, we're going to have an overview of some Blueprint

4
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.439
logic, Blueprint terminology, as well as

5
00:00:12.439 --> 00:00:13.960
some C++ terminology.

6
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.000
Don't worry, you don't need to be an expert programmer.

7
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.559
We're just going to help define

8
00:00:18.559 --> 00:00:20.160
what some of the terms mean and how

9
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.839
we use them so that everybody will be on the same page

10
00:00:22.839 --> 00:00:24.160
moving forward.

11
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.239
We're then going to go over Unreal Motion graphics or UMG

12
00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:29.839
just to give a quick overview of how it works,

13
00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:32.240
what it is, what we use it for, and how

14
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.500
it can be used to help power any user interface interaction we'd

15
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.259
like to build in our project.

16
00:00:37.259 --> 00:00:39.560
And then finally, we'll take all of the stuff

17
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.460
that we've done in this preamble

18
00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.119
and apply that to our workshop, where

19
00:00:44.119 --> 00:00:48.539
we will create a drivable car that can pick things up

20
00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:50.880
and then has a timer and a score.

21
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.539
It's going to be really, really cool.

22
00:00:52.539 --> 00:00:54.039
So let's go ahead and get started

23
00:00:54.039 --> 00:00:55.439
with our Blueprint overview.
